Description: Keel overlay: CrowdSec and its firewall bouncer
 The CrowdSec overlay of Keel Linux (handbook decisions 0029 and 0036):
 trixie's crowdsec and crowdsec-firewall-bouncer, and the overlay manifest
 keel reads, installed as /usr/share/keel/overlays/crowdsec.yaml (decision
 0041).
 .
 Both units are installed disabled and stopped, the state of a simple
 installation: the first installation of this package disables what the
 Debian packages' own maintainer scripts enabled and started, and a
 systemd preset keeps them disabled at first boot. keel spec apply turns
 them on where the instance spec says so. A unit that was already enabled
 or running before this package is left as it was.
